\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Shall I, for fear of feeble man,
\par The Spirit's course in me restrain?
\par Or, undismayed, in deed and word
\par Be a true witness for my Lord?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Saviour of men, Thy searching eye
\par Dost all my inmost thoughts descry,
\par Doth aught on earth my wishes raise,
\par Or the world's pleasures or its praise?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The love of God doth me constrain
\par To seek the wandering souls of men;
\par With cries, entreaties, tears, to save,
\par To snatch them from the gaping grave.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My life, my blood, I here present,
\par If for Thy truth they may be spent:
\par Fulfil Thy sovereign counsel, Lord;
\par Thy will be done, Thy name adored.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Give me Thy strength, O God of power;
\par Then, let wind blows or thunders roar,
\par Thy faithful witness will I be:
\par 'Tis fixed; I can do all through Thee!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

